{"id":29512,"slug":"a-ship-to-india","title":"A Ship to India","year":1947,"country":"Sweden","duration":95,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29512-a-ship-to-india","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/3dce7db1ec8339bc72cb2faf8e6761cf/F0pMocrrx0c3uEI4V1xA5FJGIsp0tX_large.jpg","description":"The hunchbacked sailor Johannes (Birger Malmsten) longs to escape his home on a salvage ship helmed by his cruel, drunken father (Holger Löwenadler)—and so does the captain himself, who is slowly going blind and planning to leave his wife and son for a music-hall performer named Sally (Gertrud Fridh). The family begins to unravel when the captain invites Sally to live on the ship, where she and Johannes form a tender connection. Told in flashback and inspired in part by French poetic realism, A Ship to India marks a major evolution in Ingmar Bergman’s early filmmaking, demonstrating his gifts as a conjurer of beguiling images and a dramatist of lacerating emotions.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Holger Löwenadler","role":"Captain Alexander Blom","slug":"holger-lowenadler"},{"actor":"Anna Lindahl","role":"Alice Blom","slug":"anna-lindahl"},{"actor":"Birger Malmsten","role":"Johannes Blom","slug":"birger-malmsten"},{"actor":"Gertrud Fridh","role":"Sally","slug":"gertrud-fridh"},{"actor":"Naemi Briese","role":"Selma","slug":"naemi-briese"},{"actor":"Hjördis Petterson","role":"Sofi","slug":"hjordis-petterson"},{"actor":"Lasse Krantz","role":"Hans","slug":"lasse-krantz"},{"actor":"Jan Molander","role":"Bertil","slug":"jan-molander"},{"actor":"Erik Hell","role":"Pekka","slug":"erik-hell"},{"actor":"Åke Fridell","role":"Variety hall owner","slug":"ake-fridell-2"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Lorens Marmstedt","slug":null},{"role":"Based on the play by","person":"Martin Söderhjelm","slug":nul